# Sandbox Hub

Several purpose-built sandboxes, defined by the **operator** in
`SANDBOX_PROFILES_FILE`, each its own tool with its own instruction and
container. Users only turn them on or off (`/sandbox`); agents opt in from the
tool picker. Admins listed in `SANDBOX_HUB_ADMINS` can edit each profile's
instruction for every user. Maintainer doc: `openwiki/architecture/sandbox.md`
(Sandbox Hub profiles, Editable instructions).

## Invariants (keep)

- **`general` is the old Sandbox.** It keeps `lobe-sandbox`, the legacy
  alias, the built-in instruction (as its starting text), and the pre-profile
  session key. Without a profiles file or a saved edit its manifest is
  byte-identical to the old static
  `SandboxManifest` (golden test in `payload.sandbox.test.ts`).
- **Profile ids:** `^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$`, ≤ 16 chars, never `_`.
  Longer ids push `lobe-sandbox--<id>____<api>____builtin` past 64 chars, where
  `ToolNameResolver` hashes names and the worker (`split('____')`) breaks.
- **Sandbox tools are appended last** to the builtin list (worker payload and
  tool-store slice), where the static manifest used to be. Do not reorder:
  it changes prompt bytes for every existing agent.
- **One gate:** every call goes through `resolveSandboxProfileForUser`. Do not
  add a path that invokes the provider without it.
- **Server details never reach the browser:** the Hub DTO has no URL, key, or
  image. Keys come from `apiKeyEnv`; a literal key in the file is rejected.
- **A broken profiles file configures nothing.** Do not "recover" by running
  the valid half; the operator would not notice the missing profile.
- **Instructions: starting text plus a shared edit.** `compose.ts` builds the
  starting text once per process; a row in `sandbox_profile_instructions`
  replaces it for **every** user until reset. No per-user or per-request text
  in an instruction. Without a saved row the prompt bytes must stay exactly
  the starting text (golden test).
- **Instruction writes are admin only.** `SandboxProfileInstructionModel` is
  not user-scoped; every write path must call `isSandboxHubAdmin` first.
- **Fail closed on reads.** Only a missing table (`42P01`) may fall back to
  defaults (choices) or the starting text (instructions). Any other read
  error is raised, never treated as "no rows".
- Hub tRPC lives in the `sandboxHub.` namespace, which is in the client's
  `VERIFIED_ACCOUNT_RPC_NAMESPACES`. A new scope-checked namespace must be
  added there too, or every call fails as a mismatched user.

## Remote servers

ChatHub reaches execd only through the lifecycle server proxy, so a dedicated
host exposes one HTTPS endpoint. OpenSandbox has no TLS and its single-tenant
proxy route is not key-checked: the reverse proxy must require
`OPEN-SANDBOX-API-KEY` on every path and allow only the ChatHub host
(`docker/opensandbox-remote/`). Server-wide settings (runtime class, egress
mode, `network_mode`, max timeout) need separate servers.

## Verify

Provider, session-key, or label changes: run `e2e.live.test.ts` 5+ times on a
local OpenSandbox (`.cursor/rules/sandbox-repro.mdc`), including the
two-profiles-in-one-conversation case, and confirm no containers are left.
